
## Architecture

These orders apply once the system is composed from plugins. The map is [docs/architecture.md](docs/architecture.md); the vocabulary is [docs/glossary.md](docs/glossary.md).

- **Compose; do not patch a core.** New behavior attaches to a documented extension point. Changing the core operation is an architecture change, and [docs/architecture.md](docs/architecture.md) updates in the same change.
- **A capability is a seam, and a seam has three roles.** Adding a capability means designing the Service Definition, at least one Provider, and the Consumer together. One role alone is not a seam.
- **Registrations are effects.** Every contribution goes through the context so it unwinds on unload, and a registry's registration returns its own disposer. Prove disposal by unloading and observing removal.
- **Depend on definitions, never on a concrete provider.** A consumer injects the service; only composition chooses the implementation.
- **Declare dependencies; never sequence by hand.** A plugin names what it requires and waits.
- **Model-visible means logged.** Anything reaching a request must be reconstructable from the durable log. A new model-visible input requires a new durable event.
- **Pick the domain before the event.** Durable facts go in the log; transient facts about work in flight go on the live domain; policy attaches to the seam it governs.
- **Waterfall listeners call the continuation.** Return without it only when you deliberately own the decision and mean to short-circuit the chain.
- **No hardcoded tunables.** A deployment-varying choice is a validated configuration field. A default constant is not configurability.
- **Enforce the decision in the operation that makes it.** A filtered list, a facade, or a listener order is not enforcement when another caller can bypass it.
- **Publish state at its commit point**, and derive caches, views, and notifications from one authoritative source.
- **Fail loud at load** when the misconfiguration is self-contained; otherwise at the earliest point it can be resolved.
